Design\GDD.md:9:- v0.22 (2026-11-12): owner's spec: **elemental build-up** (fire, lightning, ice) on every enemy, with three status effects (Ignite, Shock, Frost), per-enemy resistances and reactions, a weak-point bonus for weapon hits, and every number in data. Owner's answers: the old small 
effects on every hit (burn, the lightning slow, the enchant's chill) are **removed**; the status effect at the full bar is the only elemental effect (the ice floor keeps its zone slow). The elemental sword and the ember staff build up their element too. See §6 "Elemental build-up".
Design\GDD.md:25:- v0.6 (2026-11-12): art rule clarified for characters (style of the world they belong to); story premise; opening sequence with the first gun; starting spells; enchant only with a gun in hand; key changes (F quick-use, G interact, L1 enchant on gamepad); counter-style ammo 
refilled on era travel; automatic checkpoints; no sprint; one full-armor slot.
Design\GDD.md:27:- v0.4 (2026-11-12): weapon skill tree contents; two held slots (one gun + one staff) and how to switch; no spells with a gun except the enchant; enchant key; air passives always on; ice shield QTE; staffs from chests; sword blade is pixel art with a medieval HUD; final boss mixes 
both styles.
Design\GDD.md:28:- v0.3 (2026-11-12): art rule follows the object; the player is always pixel art; 5-spell loadout and controls; staffs and basic magic attack; gun aim; enchant has a QTE, player-chosen element, not on the sword; QTE grading and mana; two UI styles (90s RPG vs. modern cyberpunk) for 
HUD and skill trees.
Design\GDD.md:29:- v0.2 (2026-11-12): theme reading, art rule, shared map with era-gated zones, cross-era style mixing, QTE = power + reach, weapon enchant spell, skill points from encounters, enemy waves and sub-bosses, no early melee, architect definition.
Design\GDD.md:135:## 6. Magic (4 elements + weapon enchant)
Design\GDD.md:156:- **Spells can only be cast with the staff in hand.** With a gun in hand, the only spell available is the weapon enchant. To cast, the player switches to the staff mid-fight.
Design\GDD.md:164:### Weapon enchant (always equipped)
Design\GDD.md:166:- **Only usable with a gun in hand** (it enchants the gun).
Design\GDD.md:177:- **Ignite (fire, sustained damage):** fire damage at fixed time steps for the status duration. Sources: fireball, fire wall, flamethrower (on its 0.3 s damage ticks), the ember staff, the elemental sword and a fire-enchanted gun.
Design\GDD.md:178:- **Shock (lightning, interruption):** an electric discharge (a small hit of lightning damage) and the enemy's reaction: **stun** (stops moving and attacking for the duration, its attack is cancelled), **interrupt** (only cancels the attack it was winding up) or **none**. Sources: 
lightning bolt (every enemy it passes through, once each), lightning rune (enemies in its blast radius, so Expanded Sigil applies), static orb, the elemental sword and a lightning-enchanted gun.
Design\GDD.md:179:- **Frost (ice, slow and control):** the enemy's reaction: **freeze** (cannot move or attack for the duration), **slow** (a strong slow) or **none**. Sources: the **ice floor only** among spells (low build-up on each of its ticks, so standing on it fills the bar slowly and an 
ice-enchanted gun finishes it faster), the elemental sword and an ice-enchanted gun. The ice wall and the ice shield build up nothing. The ice floor's own slow (50%, Deep Freeze 55/60/65%, cap 80%, QTE) is unchanged. **Slows never stack:** when the ice floor and Frost both slow an enemy, only the 
strongest counts.

